      "amount": "2 tbsp",
      "notes": "chopped"
    }
  ],
  "instructions": [
    "Rinse the toor dal under cold running water until the water runs clear.",
    "In a medium pot, sauté the diced carrot, onion, and minced garlic in a splash of water until translucent, about 3-4 minutes.",
    "Add the rinsed dal, ground cumin, ground turmeric, salt, pepper, and vegetable broth. Bring to a boil over medium-high heat.",
    "Reduce the heat to low, cover, and simmer for 20-25 minutes, or until the dal is tender and the soup has thickened to your liking.",
    "Stir in the fresh lemon juice and zest, tasting and adjusting seasoning if necessary.",
    "Remove the pot from the heat and let the soup rest for 5 minutes to allow flavors to meld.",
    "Serve hot, garnished with a sprinkle of chopped fresh cilantro."
  ],
